codex
ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: yellow
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "SGLang", url: "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/python/sglang/srt/managers/mm_utils.py#L1244-L1256", overlap: "Shipping multimodal embedding-cache hash over processed ndarray/torch tensor features; directly implements the proposed processed-domain key."},
  {system: "vLLM", url: "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/vllm/multimodal/hasher.py#L61-L84", overlap: "Shipping hasher uses decoded pixel array for bare PIL.Image but original transport bytes for MediaWithBytes; also has EXIF ImageID UUID escape hatch."},
  {system: "vLLM", url: "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/vllm/config/multimodal.py#L123-L132", overlap: "Shipping multimodal processor cache exists and defaults to 4GB LRU, so the byte-vs-pixel key choice is on a real cache path."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/advanced/kv-cache-reuse.html", overlap: "KV-cache reuse documented, but I found no evidence in the searched docs/source snippets of processed-pixel multimodal cache-key canonicalization."},
  {system: "FlashInfer", url: "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer", overlap: "Kernel/KV-cache infrastructure; no found overlap with VLM image preprocessor cache keys."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: L0 holds for the stated synthetic/controlled workload: 320 images x 9 variants, genuine lossless re-encodes at 0% vLLM byte-key hits vs 100% SGLang processed-tensor hits, and lossy controls at 0%/0%. Realistic production materiality is insufficient evidence: the decisive constant, prevalence of lossless pixel-preserving re-encoding in real VLM-serving or agent/RAG traffic, is unmeasured; TTFT/FLOPs savings are also unmeasured. The strict gate miss on all-lossless 16.7% is not a systems kill because base64 rewrap is byte-identical and correctly hits, but it must be reported with the genuine-reencode denominator.
RATIONALE: Prompt version v001. This is not a new systems design: processed-domain hashing is already shipping in SGLang, and vLLM already has a decoded-array path plus mm_uuid/ImageID escape hatch. The useful contribution is the measured cross-system hash-domain mismatch and clean null exit, not a new cache mechanism. Yellow because the mechanism is real and reproducible enough for L0, but production scale impact depends on an unmeasured workload distribution; without named traffic prevalence and wall-time/FLOP savings, green would overclaim.
